# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads. Explicit on purpose.
#
# Without this file gcloud derives the filter from .gitignore, which makes the
# contents of every Cloud Build upload a silent dependency on .gitignore being
# correct. It was not: `secrets/` does not match `.secrets/`, so the Gmail
# refresh token would have been shipped to Cloud Build and kept in the source
# bucket. Naming the filter here means that mistake cannot repeat quietly.
#
# .gcloudignore itself must not be ignored — gcloud reads it from the upload
# root, and the Dockerfile needs the build context it describes.

# --- credentials, first and non-negotiable ------------------------------------
.secrets/
secrets/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
token_*.json
*.pem
*.p12

# --- not needed to build the image --------------------------------------------
# The Dockerfile's own .dockerignore prunes again inside the build; this only
# decides what leaves the machine.
.git/
.github/
.venv/
node_modules/
web/
docs/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.claude/

# Tests do not go in the runtime image, but they are cheap and keeping them out
# of the upload keeps the build context honest about what is being shipped.
**/tests/

emulator-data/
*.log
.pytest-all.out
